{"chunk_id": "1d3688537855", "text": "This section recounts the origin and rise of Ganapati (Ganesha) and several mythic episodes around Shiva. Parvati fashions a clay guardian, Ganapati, to protect her privacy while bathing. When Shiva returns to Kailasa and is blocked by the boy, he angrily beheads him. Parvati\u2019s grief compels Shiva to restore the child to life by attaching the head of the elephant-demon Gajasura, declaring him his son and granting him primacy in worship as Vighnesvara, remover of obstacles. Ganapati later wins lordship over the divine hosts by wisely circumambulating his parents instead of racing around the world. He is crowned, married to Siddhi and Buddhi, and honored by the gods. The chapter then turns to cosmic conflicts: the destruction of the Tripura demon cities by Shiva and the rise of the formidable demon Jalandhara.\nParvati creates Ganapati, Siva beheads then revives him with an elephant head, grants him primacy; later he wins lordship, marries Siddhi and Buddhi, and Siva destroys Tripura.\nThemes: origin of Ganesha, obedience and duty, divine repentance and restoration, wisdom over speed, destruction of Tripura", "vector": [0.007757632993161678, -0.005767631344497204, -0.002406552666798234, 0.00698861526325345, -0.010928143747150898, 0.013127264566719532, -0.024284763261675835, -0.002005179412662983, -0.023030051961541176, -0.02521567977964878, 0.01106980536133051, 0.01855086162686348, 0.0037472739350050688, 0.003635968780145049, -0.004867071285843849, 0.009896041825413704, 0.04263325408101082, -0.021492015570402145, 0.023529238998889923, 0.00660747941583395, -0.011204720474779606, 0.010442448779940605, -0.009700413793325424, -0.00600710604339838, -0.0026089258026331663, -2.9486383937182836e-05, 0.022719746455550194, -0.010523397475481033, 0.019023064523935318, -0.00474564777687192, -0.024622052907943726, -0.016783470287919044, -0.019994456321001053, -0.008486175909638405, -0.0038181045092642307, -0.0021822559647262096, -0.002403